 - Windows and the shell around them: a float can become a window of its own (the `window` place), with the same client state and a page of its own (`?float=<id>`), because a tab's state is held under its instance id; the windows share one saved arrangement, so a write is a turn taken through the main (`src/desktop/decide/save-turn.ts`, `src/lib/shell/desktop-windows.svelte.ts`). The window state, the application menu, the keys the page asks for, the folder sheet and the find bar are the app's, and the text menu and the tab menus stay oculus's own. The find bar is a view of its own because Chromium's find counts the text of a box in the page it searches (`src/desktop/windows/find-bar.ts`). The PDF of a deck is printed by a hidden window of the host (`src/desktop/windows/print.ts`) that loads only the print route of its own server, is answered no bridge channel and is no entry of the windows list, so the window file cannot record it; the page asks for it on `oculus:print-pdf`, which the host refuses for any other address. The audience window of a presentation is the second window of that kind (`src/desktop/windows/show.ts`): `linkDecision` names the server's `/present/show` address with exactly `root` and `path` as its own kind, `route` of `windows.ts` hands it to the audience module instead of the default browser, `senderOf` gives its page the `audience` sender and `mayCall` answers it no channel, and it is no entry of the windows list and no record of the window file, so it is not restored at the next start. One window is open per deck, and asking again loads its address again and brings it forward, so a presenter screen that started after a reload meets a live page. It opens on a display other than the asking window's in simple full screen, or beside the asking window when there is one display (`audiencePlace` of `decide/place.ts`), is granted full screen by the permission handlers, sends a slide's link to the default browser, closes with the window that asked for it, and closes by Close Window while it has the focus. What the app adds for a reader is in `docs/window.md` ("The window and the app").
