 Machine-local values live in `config/local.yml` of the engine directory the server was given, which for the checkout is `tools/oculus/config/local.yml`; it is gitignored and optional: `hub` is the absolute path of the research hub, defaulting to two directories above the engine; `port` is an integer, defaulting to 8790; and `claude_bin` names the Claude CLI used by update tasks and by the prompts of schedules, defaulting to `claude` on PATH. That file is read by itself and is never merged with the rest of the folder, so a key it carries is the machine's own and no other reader sees it. The server reads no environment variable of its own except the operating system's `SHELL`, the command a plain terminal starts (`/bin/zsh` when the environment names none): a run that must not touch the checkout's configuration is started over a copy with `--engine`.
 
